## Separation and precedence

`corex/core` owns portable context/contracts and cannot depend on `flex/*`; `corex/tenancy` is the only Stancl adapter; `corex/auth` remains optional from tenancy's perspective. Root management bookkeeping (`root_identity_accounts.sync_status`) is not a tenant projector or a central business writer. Tenant projection writes only the target account user row via tenancy context; it may not write root tables from tenant code.

D40 is controlling: no CRM signup, registration, invitation, account creation, grant, acceptance, or revoke writer is introduced by these candidate bindings. FLEXID/P6.26 owns central identity and switcher behavior; FLEX-2 P6.25 owns paid provisioning/control-plane operations. Therefore all six bindings are separable documentation readiness, not package acceptance.
